-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Everyone's a Wally
  Publisher   Mikro-Gen, 1985
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Everyone's a Wally (1985)(Mikro-Gen).z80
  MD5         6a314faecd0b5e52ad9ef612d72e214f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Characters painted as people: Wally in a light-blue jacket and
              blue trousers with a grey cap and pink face, others with their
              own hair, skin and clothes colours. Source: enhanced colours
              from an older Spec256 conversion (the EmuZWin games package),
              painter not established.

  Pace        original (-0.13% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same start
              state; probe 0xE79F, Sinclair keys given at the game's reads, R
              fixed at the audit's four sites in both arms; game state, 90
              addresses, equal at every update)

  Changes     1.1: works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11); the hooks hand
              back the CPU speed the game was running at
              1.2: the game now holds the original's pace; 1.1 ran up to 4%
              slow in quiet rooms.

  Note        Known issues: pace against the original in JNext, 2026-11-08, 8
              runs with the same input and game state equal at every update,
              default and Enhanced: overall -0.20 to -0.10%, quiet scenes
              -0.22 to -0.11%, busy scenes -0.15 to -0.05%, stretches of 20
              updates -0.6 to +0.2% (1.1: overall +0.3 to +2.2%, quiet up to
              +3.9%, slowest stretch +5.5%). A yellow figure stays on the
              TOUGH LUCK game over screen and the control menu after it (not
              in the plain build). The game's random numbers come from R and
              differ from the original's with the same keys, as in 1.0 and
              1.1. Missing: the Enhanced set was carried over from Dean's
              build and not replayed on its own (its bytes are 1.0's, on the
              new hooks); puzzles not reached in testing (few rooms walked);
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Change character anywhere

